s\":[\"reliable sources for Wikipedia\",\"independent sources Wikipedia\",\"Wikipedia citation research\",\"Wikipedia notability sources\",\"Wikipedia article sources\"],\"hasPart\":{\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can company websites be used as Wikipedia sources?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Company websites are primary or self-published sources about the subject. They may be useful for limited, uncontroversial facts in some cases, but they are usually weak evidence for notability and should not replace independent secondary coverage.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Are news articles always reliable?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Not automatically. Reliability depends on the publication, editorial standards, and the type of claim. Reputable outlets are often useful, but each source should still be evaluated in context.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How many sources are needed for a Wikipedia page?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"There is no fixed number that guarantees eligibility. The key issue is whether reliable, independent sources provide significant coverage and support the article’s content. Quality, independence, and relevance matter more than a raw count.\"}}]}}24:[[[\"$\",\"script\",\"0\",{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https://schema.org\\\",\\\"@type\\\":\\\"WebPage\\\",\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog/reliable-sources-for-wikipedia#webpage\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"What Are Reliable Sources for Wikipedia?\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"A clear guide to reliable, independent sources on Wikipedia, including what usually works, what to avoid, and how to evaluate coverage quality.\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog/reliable-sources-for-wikipedia\\\",\\\"isPartOf\\\":{\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https://miqllcwiki.com/#website\\\"},\\\"about\\\":{\\\"@id\\\":\\\